# Assets

Rules for files under `app/assets/`. Follow global rules in `global.mdc`.

## Purpose

`assets/` holds files Vite processes: SCSS, fonts, icons, and images. Use `public/` for files that need a fixed URL.

## Directory structure

```
app/assets/
├── styles/
│   ├── app.scss              # Entry: loads layers in order
│   ├── base/                 # Tokens, type, reset, containers, animations
│   ├── utils/                # Mixins and helper classes
│   ├── layouts/              # Shell styles
│   ├── components/           # Shared UI styles
│   ├── pages/                # Route styles
│   └── vendors/              # Third-party overrides
├── font/                     # Self-hosted fonts (.gitkeep until files are added)
├── icons/                    # Icon assets
└── img/                      # Images, grouped by feature
```

| Folder | Current starter |
|--------|-----------------|
| `styles/` | Layered SCSS. No UI-framework import. |
| `font/` | Empty. Add files here, then `@font-face` in `base/_typography.scss`. |
| `icons/` | Icon CSS or SVG. Do not add a vendor set until the app uses it. |
| `img/` | Feature folders such as `img/auth/`. Prefer SVG. |

## Style entry

`app/assets/styles/app.scss` loads layers in this order:

```scss
@use 'base/index' as base;
@use 'utils/index' as utils;
@use 'layouts/index' as layouts;
@use 'components/index' as components;
@use 'pages/index' as pages;
@use 'vendors/index' as vendors;
```

**Order:** base → utils → layouts → components → pages → vendors.

Wire the file from `nuxt.config.ts` when global styles should ship:

```ts
export default defineNuxtConfig({
  css: ['~/assets/styles/app.scss'],
})
```

Install `sass` before that import. Do not import a UI kit that is not a dependency.

## Partials

- Prefix partials with `_` (`_variables.scss`, `_buttons.scss`).
- Each layer folder has `index.scss` that `@use`s its partials.
- Use `@use` and `@forward`. Do not use `@import`.
- `base/index.scss` forwards variables. `utils/index.scss` forwards mixins.

```scss
@use '../base/variables' as *;

.btn {
  background-color: $primary;
}
```

| Layer | Starter files | Add here |
|-------|---------------|----------|
| `base/` | variables, typography, containers, framework, animations | Tokens, reset, type |
| `utils/` | mixins, helpers | Breakpoints, flex helpers, utility classes |
| `layouts/` | `_shell.scss` (`.app-shell`) | Navbar, sidebar, overlays |
| `components/` | `_buttons.scss` (`.btn`) | Cards, forms, tables |
| `pages/` | `_page.scss` (`.page-wrapper`) | Styles for one route |
| `vendors/` | Comment-only index | Overrides for an installed library |

- Put a rule in the lowest layer that owns it.
- Do not add page rules to `base/` or `app.scss`.

### Tokens

Colors, text, background, icon size, and card shadow live in `base/_variables.scss`. Use those variables instead of raw hex values in new partials.

## Images, fonts, icons

- Images: `app/assets/img/{feature}/{name}.svg`, referenced as `~/assets/img/{feature}/{name}.svg`.
- Fonts: `app/assets/font/`. Declare them in `base/_typography.scss`. The starter uses the system font stack until files are added.
- Icons: `app/assets/icons/`. Import a vendor stylesheet only after that library is part of the app.

## `assets/` vs `public/`

| Location | Use for |
|----------|---------|
| `app/assets/` | Styles, fonts, and images imported from Vue or SCSS |
| `public/` | `robots.txt`, favicons, files served from a fixed path |

## Naming

- SCSS partials: `_kebab-case.scss`
- Images: `kebab-case.svg`
- Folders: plural or a feature name (`font/`, `img/auth/`, `styles/components/`)

## What not to put in assets

- Vue components (`app/components/`).
- API logic.
- `*.Zone.Identifier` metadata.
- Duplicate copies of the same image.
- Large binaries when SVG or a compressed format is enough.

## Adding a partial

1. Create `_my-feature.scss` in the right layer.
2. `@use` it from that layer's `index.scss`.
3. Keep tokens in `base/` and mixins in `utils/`.
4. Scope page selectors (`.page-wrapper`, `.auth-page`) so they do not leak.
